<%# locals: () %>

<dialog
  data-dialog-target="dialog"
  data-action="click->dialog#backdropClose"
  class="cn-dialog border-0 p-0 rounded-4 shadow-lg"
  style="max-width: 32rem;"
>
  <div class="p-4">
    <div class="d-flex justify-content-between align-items-start mb-3">
      <h1 class="fs-5 fw-bold mb-0">
        <i class="bi bi-info-circle me-2"></i>
        How to play
      </h1>
      <button
        type="button"
        class="btn-close"
        data-action="dialog#close"
        aria-label="Close"
      ></button>
    </div>

    <p class="text-secondary small">
      This app runs the spectrum cards, the hidden target, turn order, and
      scoring. The psychic types a clue and the whole table sees it.
    </p>

    <div class="d-flex gap-3 mb-3">
      <i class="bi bi-eye-fill fs-4 text-secondary"></i>
      <div>
        <div class="fw-semibold">The psychic (one per turn)</div>
        <p class="mb-0 small text-secondary">
          Only you see the hidden target on the dial. Type
          <strong>a clue</strong> that places your concept between the two ends
          of the spectrum. Once you send it, you can't give any more hints —
          your team takes it from there.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="d-flex gap-3 mb-3">
      <i class="bi bi-sliders fs-4 text-secondary"></i>
      <div>
        <div class="fw-semibold">The team</div>
        <p class="mb-0 small text-secondary">
          Discuss the clue, drag the dial to where you think the target sits,
          and <strong>Lock it in</strong>. Closer is better:
          <strong>4</strong> points for a bullseye, then <strong>3</strong> and
          <strong>2</strong> for the outer bands.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="d-flex gap-3 mb-3">
      <i class="bi bi-arrow-left-right fs-4 text-secondary"></i>
      <div>
        <div class="fw-semibold">The other team</div>
        <p class="mb-0 small text-secondary">
          Before the reveal, guess whether the target's center is to the
          <strong>left</strong> or <strong>right</strong> of the locked dial —
          unless the team nailed the bullseye, which leaves you nothing to
          catch. Get it right and you score <strong>1</strong> point.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="d-flex gap-3">
      <i class="bi bi-trophy-fill fs-4 text-secondary"></i>
      <div>
        <div class="fw-semibold">Goal</div>
        <p class="mb-0 small text-secondary">
          The team that goes second starts with a <strong>1</strong>-point head
          start to even the odds. The first team to reach <strong>10</strong>
          points wins.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</dialog>
